                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Out-of-date red tape has kneecapped Medicare and Medicaid patients\u2019 ability to effectively use online booking platforms for their health services. These platforms are regulated by ambiguous pre-Internet Age laws that complicate booking for providers and limit innovation and widespread use. That's why I introduced the Health ACCESS Act with @RepSchneider to clear the way for patients to use 21st-century tools to interact with their health providers. Read more about it here:\n\nhttps://t.co/geXVmgbMrc",
